# Scripts, container configuration and strict text formats are read by Linux
# shells, containers and CI runners. A checkout with core.autocrlf=true would hand
# them a carriage return at the end of the shebang, and every start would fail on
# an invisible character. The store archive refuses CRLF as well
# (scripts/release/store-archive.sh).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
